Smart Parking Availability Prediction using Machine Learning

Project Overview

Smart Parking Availability Prediction is a machine learning-based project designed to help users understand parking availability through an interactive web dashboard.

The project uses a trained machine learning model and parking dataset to provide a dashboard-based interface for exploring parking availability.

Technologies Used

* Python
* Machine Learning
* Streamlit
* Pandas
* Joblib
* Scikit-learn

Project Files

* main.py – Main Streamlit dashboard application
* inspect_data.py – Data inspection script
* inspect_model.py – Model inspection script
* parking_data.csv – Parking dataset
* parking_model.pkl – Saved machine learning model
* requirements.txt – Required Python libraries

Features

* Interactive web dashboard using Streamlit
* Loads parking data from a CSV file
* Loads a trained machine learning model
* Displays parking availability information

Installation and Setup

1. Clone this repository:

git clone https://github.com/Anujavibhute/smart_parking_prediction.git

2. Navigate to the project folder:

cd smart_parking_prediction

3. Install the required libraries:

pip install -r requirements.txt

4. Run the application:

streamlit run main.py

Project Objective

The objective of this project is to explore the use of machine learning in parking availability prediction and provide an interactive dashboard for presenting the results.

